Z||000000||kanada||04-12-2001||09:32 PM||||the pontiac 6000 engine apparently fits my fiero but i've been told the starter is on the wrong side.<P>the engine is a code x <P>is it still possible, and if so what problems will araise<P>i've also been told the heads have to be changed, but others have told me they should be the same<P>the 6000 engine is carburated but i can purchase this low mileaged engines at a steal||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||04-12-2001||10:39 PM||||That is a front wheel drive and the starter is on the correct side already.  To make sure, I looked it up in my trusty chiltons manual for the 'A' platform carline.  If you look at the car, the starter should be on the front of the eng whether it is in the 6000 or the Fiero.<BR>BTW what year is the car? my book doesn't show and eng code 'X' for '82 thru '95.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-12-2001||10:46 PM||||You really don't want a carbed engine if you can avoid it. Nearly all the stock GM engines that can be shoved in a Fiero are cheap. shop around. ||||reg||1
